createdate":"2015-12-16 08:10:30","stars":"3"},{"reviewbody":"Thanks to Noise-Arch for sharing this piece.  It is composed by me - Darren Copeland - in 1989.  It represents for me a transition from working with analog synths to working with environmental sounds.  The latter of which became more of a focus since the time of this piece.  The piece was originally composed for a theatre production by Actor’s Lab Theatre in Toronto. Much thanks to Richard Nieoczym for his guidance and confidence.  Examples of my work can be found at electrocd.com and darrencopeland.net","reviewtitle":"Notes from Darren Copeland","reviewer":"Darren Copeland","reviewer_itemname":"@darren_copeland","reviewdate":"2018-10-26 16:12:42","createdate":"2018-10-26 16:12:42","stars":"0"}],"server":"ia800502.us.archive.org","uniq":1077681829,"workable_servers":["ia800502.us.archive.org","ia600502.us.archive.org"]}